+# USDC Pay
+
+A small production-style dApp with a `/pay` page: connect a wallet, enter a
+recipient (address or ENS) and an amount, and send **USDC on Ethereum mainnet**.
+The page shows your USDC balance and your ETH balance (for gas), each with live
+USD value.
+
+USDC is the real mainnet token:
+[`0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`](https://etherscan.io/token/0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48)
+— 6 decimals, handled faithfully throughout.
+
+## Stack
+
+- **Next.js 14** (App Router, TypeScript)
+- **wagmi v2 + viem v2** — typed contract reads/writes
+- **RainbowKit v2** — wallet connection, network switching, address/ENS UI
+- **TanStack Query** — data/cache layer (via wagmi)
+- **Chainlink** ETH/USD + USDC/USD feeds, read onchain — no third-party price API or key
+
+## Getting started
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill in the two values
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000  ->  /pay
+```
+
+### Environment
+
+| Variable | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL` | Dedicated mainnet RPC (Alchemy/Infura/your node). Falls back to a rate-limited public endpoint for local dev only. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | WalletConnect project id from [cloud.reown.com](https://cloud.reown.com). Enables mobile/WalletConnect wallets; injected wallets work without it. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` | Absolute production URL, used to make Open Graph image/URLs absolute. |
+
+Scripts: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run start`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`.
+
+## How it works
+
+- **Balances** — ETH via `useBalance`, USDC via `balanceOf`. Both refetch on new
+  blocks and immediately after a transfer confirms.
+- **USD context** — every amount (balances, live input, confirmation summary)
+  shows `~$` value from onchain Chainlink feeds.
+- **Recipient** — accepts a hex address or an ENS name. Validates, normalizes
+  pasted input, resolves ENS forward (name→address) and reverse (address→name).
+- **Send** — a single ERC-20 `transfer` (you own the tokens, so no approval step).
+  Amount is parsed with `parseUnits(value, 6)`; never raw base units.
+
+### The four-state action button (one primary action at a time)
+
+1. **Not connected** → `Connect Wallet`
+2. **Wrong network** → `Switch to Ethereum` (checked before anything else)
+3. **Ready** → `Send N USDC`, enabled only with a valid recipient + amount
+
+While sending, the button is disabled the entire time and shows the live phase:
+`Confirm in your wallet…` (waiting for signature) → `Sending USDC…` (waiting for
+on-chain confirmation). It re-enables only after the receipt resolves. Errors are
+translated to plain language (wallet rejection, insufficient gas, onchain revert)
+and shown inline; success links to Etherscan.
+
+## Design notes / frontend-ux rules applied
+
+- **Per-action pending state** — the send button owns its own submitting +
+  confirming states; released in `finally` so a wallet rejection never locks it.
+- **Fresh onchain state** — balances/allowance-equivalents come from chain reads,
+  not stale local state; balances refetch on success.
+- **Address UX** — RainbowKit account/connect components + custom validation, ENS,
+  paste normalization, and Etherscan links.
+- **USD context everywhere** amounts appear.
+- **RPC reliability** — dedicated RPC via env, batched multicalls, price polling
+  at 60s (slow-moving) and wagmi's block-based balance refresh.
+- **Theme** — semantic CSS tokens, light/dark via `prefers-color-scheme`; no
+  hardcoded dark page wrapper. RainbowKit's modal follows the same theme.
+- **Contract error translation** — `lib/errors.ts` maps wallet/RPC/revert errors
+  to human messages with a safe fallback.
+- **Metadata** — title, description, favicon, and absolute OG/Twitter tags set.
+
+### Known follow-up
+
+- The social preview image is an SVG (`public/og.svg`). It renders in-app and as
+  an absolute URL; some social scrapers prefer PNG/JPG, so before a real launch
+  export it to PNG and point the OG/Twitter `images` at it.
